# =============================================================================
# FALCON V2 - ArduPlane SITL parameter profile V1
# =============================================================================
# Owner: controls-integration. Task:
# SENSOR_MODEL_AND_ARDUPLANE_SITL_PREPARATION (2026-08-27).
#
# Full provenance / classification for every value (and every value
# deliberately EXCLUDED) below:
#   docs/source_of_truth/autopilot/SITL_PARAM_MIGRATION.md
#
# Format: ArduPilot's own Tools/autotest/default_params/*.parm convention -
# whitespace-separated NAME VALUE, "#" comment lines - the format
# pymavlink/mavparm.py's load() (used by sim_vehicle.py --add-param-file)
# actually parses. Deliberately NOT the real aircraft's comma-CSV GCS-export
# format (docs/source_of_truth/autopilot/real_aircraft/yeni_pixhawk.param) -
# that file is a different, GCS-side export convention and is NEVER modified
# or copied wholesale.
#
# DOES NOT include: RC calibration hardware specifics, INS/COMPASS/BARO
# device IDs and calibration offsets, BRD/CAN/SERIAL hardware config, stale
# BATT_* values, the old no-pitot ARSPD_TYPE=0 config, TECS/NAVL1/EK3/AHRS/
# GPS/FLTMODE/FENCE/ARMING/AFS groups (all REVIEW_AND_ADAPT or
# DROP_OR_DO_NOT_IMPORT - see the migration doc). No PID is retuned, no
# autotune is executed by writing this file.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Roll/Pitch rate controller - FALCON_V2_MANUFACTURER_INITIAL_PID
# (Titan Dynamics Falcon V2 Build & User Manual Rev 1.0-sourced values, given
# directly by the project owner for this task - see migration doc sec 1).
# NEVER labeled FINAL_TUNED_PID or FLIGHT_VALIDATED_FINAL_PID. Autotune is
# NOT executed by this file - AUTOTUNE_LEVEL is recorded as the
# manufacturer-recommended starting point only.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
RLL_RATE_P    0.25
RLL_RATE_I    0.125
RLL_RATE_D    0.002
RLL_RATE_FF   0.125
PTCH_RATE_P   0.25
PTCH_RATE_I   0.125
PTCH_RATE_D   0.002
PTCH_RATE_FF  0.125
# MANUFACTURER_RECOMMENDED_AUTOTUNE_LEVEL - not executed this stage.
AUTOTUNE_LEVEL 8

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Servo function mapping - REAL_PARAM_CONFIGURATION, CONFIRMED against
# installed ArduPlane 4.8.0-dev libraries/SRV_Channel/SRV_Channel.h enum
# (k_aileron=4, k_elevator=19, k_rudder=21, k_throttleLeft=73,
# k_throttleRight=74). Channel numbers 1-5 kept identical to the real
# aircraft's own wiring (migration doc sec 2) - not renumbered.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SERVO1_FUNCTION   4
SERVO1_MIN        800
SERVO1_MAX        2200
SERVO1_TRIM       1500
SERVO1_REVERSED   1

SERVO2_FUNCTION   19
SERVO2_MIN        800
SERVO2_MAX        2200
SERVO2_TRIM       1500
SERVO2_REVERSED   0

SERVO3_FUNCTION   73
SERVO3_MIN        1000
SERVO3_MAX        2000
SERVO3_TRIM       1000
SERVO3_REVERSED   0

SERVO4_FUNCTION   21
SERVO4_MIN        800
SERVO4_MAX        2200
SERVO4_TRIM       1500
SERVO4_REVERSED   1

SERVO5_FUNCTION   74
SERVO5_MIN        1000
SERVO5_MAX        2000
SERVO5_TRIM       1000
SERVO5_REVERSED   0

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PTCH_TRIM_DEG - ARDUPLANE_FBWA_LEVEL_PITCH_REFERENCE_CORRECTION (2026-08-28).
# FBWA / stabilized-mode neutral-pitch-stick attitude-target OFFSET in degrees.
# Semantics CONFIRMED from ArduPlane source (V4.8.0-dev, ArduPilot commit
# 409226a637 / ArduPilot-4.6.0-beta1-7902-g409226a637, installed at
# /home/emirhan/gazebo_sim/ardupilot):
#   ArduPlane/Attitude.cpp:244  demanded_pitch = nav_pitch_cd
#                                 + int32_t(g.pitch_trim * 100.0)
#                                 + k_throttle_scaled * g.kff_throttle_to_pitch
#   ArduPlane/Parameters.cpp:651-657  GSCALAR(pitch_trim,"PTCH_TRIM_DEG",0.0f)
#                                      range -45..45, User:Standard
# Applied UNCONDITIONALLY inside stabilize_pitch_get_pitch_out() (no airspeed
# / mode / FBWA_TDRAG gate); KFF_THR2PTCH is 0 (ArduPlane default, not set in
# this file) so the throttle term is zero. FBWA (ModeFBWA::run -> Mode::run
# -> Plane::stabilize_pitch, mode.cpp:274) at neutral stick has
# nav_pitch_cd = 0, so the pitch controller then targets AHRS pitch =
# PTCH_TRIM_DEG. It is a CONTROLLER DEMAND OFFSET only - it does NOT touch the
# AHRS/EKF attitude estimate. It does NOT affect MANUAL: ModeManual::run()
# (mode_manual.cpp:17-20) calls only reset_controllers(), never
# stabilize_pitch() - MANUAL stays pure stick->servo passthrough.
# Note: with PTCH_TRIM_DEG != 0, GCS ATTITUDE.pitch is reported as
# (true_pitch - PTCH_TRIM_DEG) unless FLIGHT_OPTIONS bit 8 GCS_REMOVE_TRIM_PITCH
# is set (GCS_MAVLink_Plane.cpp:139-141) - reporting only, physics unchanged.
# NAV_CONTROLLER_OUTPUT.nav_pitch stays raw nav_pitch_cd*0.01 (= 0 at neutral).
# VALUE = +2.49 deg: the MEASURED straight-and-level nose-up pitch attitude of
# this airframe+aero+propulsion model, C.2 pitch* = +2.487 deg from
# docs/test_results/2026-08-28_ardupilot_longitudinal_equilibrium_and_sink_
# root_cause_validation.md (V* 18.162 m/s, throttle* 0.4957, elevator* +4.092
# deg, alpha* 2.472 deg, world_vz +0.005 m/s, 14/14 acceptance). NOT +3.43
# (the C.1 stale-reference settled pitch - wrong). Full provenance:
# docs/source_of_truth/autopilot/SITL_PARAM_MIGRATION.md sec 17.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PTCH_TRIM_DEG    2.49

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Simulated pitot - SITL_REQUIRED / SIMULATION_ADDED_PITOT_SENSOR. The real
# Falcon V2 had NO pitot (old ARSPD_TYPE=0 in yeni_pixhawk.param) - this is a
# NEW simulation-only capability, not a real-flight-proven sensor.
# ARSPD_TYPE=100 (SITL backend) CONFIRMED exact via installed AP_Airspeed.h
# enum TYPE_SITL=100 - not ambiguous, no PID_MAPPING_REVIEW_REQUIRED-style
# flag needed for this value. Wiring PitotSystem.cc's differential pressure
# into AP::sitl()->state.airspeed_raw_pressure is NEXT-STAGE work, not done
# by this file (migration doc sec 4/16).
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARSPD_TYPE      100
ARSPD_USE       1

# AIRSPEED_MIN/CRUISE/MAX - GAZEBO_VALIDATION, SIMULATION_DERIVED_FROM_
# GAZEBO_ENVELOPE (docs/test_results/2026-08-27_flight_envelope_validation.md).
# 12.5 m/s (moment-infeasible trim) is NEVER used as MIN. 30 m/s is NOT used
# as MAX just because it numerically worked once - 28 m/s (a
# PROVISIONAL_EDGE_ENVELOPE point with margin) is used instead.
AIRSPEED_MIN      16
AIRSPEED_CRUISE   18
AIRSPEED_MAX      28
# DATA_REQUIRED - no validated stall speed exists in this repository's
# Gazebo test results. Left at ArduPlane's own default (0 = unused),
# matching the real .param's own value (also 0) - not a regression, not a
# fabricated number.
AIRSPEED_STALL    0

# =============================================================================
# SIMULATION ENVIRONMENT - SITL ORIGIN / ALTITUDE DATUM
# =============================================================================
# Owner: controls-integration. Stage:
# SITL_ATMOSPHERE_AND_PITOT_INTEGRATION_VALIDATION (2026-09-02).
# Closes validation MAJOR-1
# (docs/validation/2026-09-02_ardupilot_tecs_and_cruise_speed_hold_validation.md
# sec 2). Full derivation + live before/after evidence:
# docs/source_of_truth/autopilot/SITL_ATMOSPHERE_AND_AIRSPEED.md
#
# These are SITL-simulator parameters (SIM_*), NOT aircraft parameters. They
# exist only inside the simulator and have no counterpart on the real vehicle.
# They set NO PID, NO TECS value, NO aerodynamic/propulsion quantity.
#
# ROOT CAUSE THEY FIX (source-cited, ArduPilot commit 409226a637):
#   The launch scripts passed `-O 0,0,0,0`. That flag IS parsed
#   (SITL_cmdline.cpp:471-472 -> :646-658), but
#   libraries/AP_HAL_SITL/SITL_cmdline.cpp:761-766 inside parse_home()
#   contains:
#       if (loc.lat == 0 && loc.lng == 0) {
#           // default to CMAC instead of middle of the ocean...
#           loc.lat = -35.363261*1e7; loc.lng = 149.165230*1e7;
#           loc.alt = 584*100;
#       }
#   i.e. a lat/lng of exactly 0,0 SILENTLY REWRITES THE ALTITUDE TOO, to the
#   584 m CMAC field elevation. The requested alt=0 was discarded. Yaw is
#   parsed after the guard, which is why the banner read
#   "Home: -35.363261 149.165230 alt=584.000000m hdg=0.000000".
#
# Consequence chain that produced the observed 673 m / EAS2TAS 1.033:
#   1. SIM_Aircraft.cpp:80-95 set_start_location() -> home/origin alt = 584 m
#   2. AP_Baro.cpp:1015-1024 update_field_elevation() auto-sets
#      _field_elevation_active = origin.alt*0.01 = 584 m
#   3. AP_Baro.h:106 get_altitude_AMSL() = (height above boot ground) +
#      _field_elevation_active = 89 + 584 = 673 m
#   4. AP_Baro_atmosphere.cpp:299-304 _get_EAS2TAS() ->
#      get_air_density_for_alt_amsl(673) = 1.148 kg/m^3 -> EAS2TAS = 1.033
#   while the Gazebo aerodynamics plugin uses a FIXED rho = 1.225 kg/m^3
#   (docs/source_of_truth/aerodynamics/aero_v1_config.yaml, ISA sea level)
#   and the test worlds declare <elevation>0.0</elevation>.
#
# FIX: do NOT pass -O at all. With no -O, home_is_set stays false and
# SIM_Aircraft.cpp:694-707 Aircraft::update_home() builds the origin directly
# from these SIM_OPOS_* parameters - a code path with NO CMAC substitution,
# so lat=0/lng=0/alt=0 is honoured exactly.
#
# VALUES:
#
#   SIM_OPOS_ALT = 0  -- THE VALUE THIS STAGE ACTUALLY CHANGES.
#     Taken verbatim from the test worlds' own <spherical_coordinates>
#     <elevation>0.0</elevation> (e.g. tests/gazebo/worlds/
#     falcon_v2_ardupilot_basic_closed_loop_flight_world.sdf:64), and
#     consistent with the fixed rho = 1.225 kg/m^3 (ISA SEA LEVEL) that
#     docs/source_of_truth/aerodynamics/aero_v1_config.yaml uses for every
#     aerodynamic force. This establishes the datum relationship, which is now
#     explicit and checkable:
#         ArduPlane altitude AMSL (m)  ==  Gazebo world z (m, ENU, +up)
#     LIVE-VERIFIED 2026-09-02: SITL banner "Home: -35.363261 149.165230
#     alt=0.000000m hdg=0.000000" (was alt=584.000000m).
#     Provenance class: SIMULATION_DATUM_ALIGNMENT (read off the world file,
#     not invented).
#
#   SIM_OPOS_LAT / SIM_OPOS_LNG = CMAC (-35.363261, 149.165230)
#     DELIBERATELY UNCHANGED from the value every prior validated stage
#     actually ran at, so that this stage changes the ALTITUDE datum ONLY and
#     nothing else (SITL's synthetic compass field and declination are derived
#     from home lat/lng; moving them would perturb the EKF for no physical
#     gain). The horizontal datum has NO effect on any Falcon V2 physics: the
#     aerodynamics, propulsion, actuator and pitot plugins are all local-frame,
#     and no Gazebo GPS/NavSat output is in the ArduPilot loop (the JSON FDM
#     backend synthesises GPS from home + local position - see
#     docs/source_of_truth/autopilot/SITL_TRANSPORT_AND_ACTUATOR_MAPPING.md).
#     WHY NOT 0,0 (which is what the world declares): ArduPilot cannot
#     represent a vehicle at exactly lat=0/lng=0/alt=0 -
#     AP_Common/Location.h:198 `initialised()` returns
#     (lat != 0 || lng != 0 || alt != 0), and AP_AHRS.cpp:492-494 raises
#     `AP_HAL::panic("uninitialised location returned by _get_location")` on a
#     SITL build. This was LIVE-REPRODUCED on 2026-09-02 with
#     SIM_OPOS_LAT/LNG/ALT all 0: ArduPlane booted, printed
#     "Home: 0.000000 0.000000 alt=0.000000m hdg=0.000000", then panicked.
#     KNOWN, RECORDED, HARMLESS DISCREPANCY: the worlds declare
#     latitude_deg/longitude_deg 0.0 while SITL uses CMAC. Only the ALTITUDE
#     datum is physically meaningful here and it is now aligned exactly.
#     No real Falcon V2 flight-site georeference exists - DATA_REQUIRED; when
#     one is supplied, set these three and the worlds' <spherical_coordinates>
#     from it together.
#
#   SIM_OPOS_HDG = 0
#     Matches the worlds' <heading_deg>0.0</heading_deg> AND the heading every
#     prior run actually used (the old `-O 0,0,0,0` yaw field WAS honoured -
#     it is parsed after the CMAC guard - so all prior stages ran at hdg 0,
#     not at the SIM_OPOS_HDG firmware default of 353). Explicitly restated
#     here so dropping -O changes nothing about heading.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIM_OPOS_LAT    -35.363261
SIM_OPOS_LNG    149.165230
SIM_OPOS_ALT    0
SIM_OPOS_HDG    0
